# WCS PostgreSQL Persistence

Persistence covers Axon events/tokens, projections, configuration/operational entities and Liquibase-managed schema.

```mermaid
flowchart TB
  cmd[Command] --> agg[Aggregate]
  agg --> event[(JPA event store)]
  event --> token[(JPA token store)]
  event --> proc[Tracking processor]
  proc --> proj[ProjectorService]
  proj --> views[(Projection tables)]
  query[Query handler] --> views
```

`AxonJpaConfig` creates a JPA `EventStorageEngine` and `JpaTokenStore`. It selects a SQL Server event storage builder only when the JDBC URL contains `sqlserver`; otherwise it uses JPA. Gap settings are `tes.axon.jpa.max-gap-offset` (1000) and `tes.axon.jpa.gap-cleaning-threshold` (100).

Root JPA settings include custom physical naming, batch size 100, ordered inserts/updates and `open-in-view: false`.

Schema/bootstrap sources:

- `tes-app/src/main/resources/db/changelog/`
- `resources/sql/create_database.sql`
- `resources/sql/entrypoint.sh`
- `resources/sql/tes_indexes.sql`
- `resources/sql/tes_indexes_validation.sql`

Projection infrastructure: `ProjectorService`, `BaseProjectionRepository`, domain `*Projector` classes and JPA views.

Related: [[WCS Axon Aggregates]], [[WCS Sagas Projections]], [[TES Deployment Architecture]].

Source: `tes-common/src/main/java/com/onomatic/tes/common/axon/AxonJpaConfig.java`; `tes-common/src/main/java/com/onomatic/tes/common/projector/persistence/`; `tes-app/src/main/resources/application.yaml`.
